<title>UK: Royal Bank makes venture capital move into France.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank makes venture capital move into France.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Bank Development Capital, part of Britain's Royal Bank of Scotland, said on Sunday it had invested nine million pounds ($14.7 million) in a 12.3 percent stake in French venture capital firm Siparex.</p>
<p>Royal Bank said the move was part of its drive into Europe. It said Siparex had invested 1.3 billion francs in many countries and had shareholders including Michelin and Lyonnaise Banque.</p>
<p>Siparex is quoted on the French stock exchange and is based in Lyon, with offices in Paris, Nantes and Besancon.</p>
<p>($ = 0.610 British Pounds)</p>
